          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Regular summer storms",
          "set": {
            "summerRain": 50
          },
          "source": "assumption"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How do you water your garden in summer?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Only when it's very dry",
          "set": {
            "gardenUse": 100
          }
        },
        {
          "label": "Not sure / by hand most days",
          "set": {
            "gardenUse": 200
          },
          "quote": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "Sprinklers or a big garden",
          "set": {
            "gardenUse": 350
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "explain": [
    {
      "shot": "establish",
      "caption": "Will a rainwater tank keep your garden green all summer?"
    },
    {
      "shot": "follow",
      "focus": "rain",
      "caption": "Rain lands on your roof and runs into the gutters."
    },
    {
      "shot": "follow",
      "focus": "collected",
      "caption": "Most of it flows down the pipe into your tank."
    },
    {
      "shot": "follow",
      "focus": "watering",
      "caption": "You water the garden from the tank instead of the tap."
    },
    {
      "shot": "cause",
      "focus": "collected",
      "drive": "summerRain",
      "caption": "More rain fills the tank faster. When full, it overflows."
    },
    {
      "shot": "turn",
      "focus": "tankNode",
      "caption": "But in summer, the garden drinks far faster than rain refills."
    },
    {
      "shot": "timelapse",
      "focus": "tankNode",
      "caption": "So the tank drains day by day until it runs dry."
    },
    {
      "shot": "follow",
      "focus": "tap",
      "caption": "Once it's empty, tap water takes over for the rest of summer."
    },
    {
      "shot": "handoff",
      "caption": "Now make it yours. Answer a few questions."
    }
  ],
  "simulate": {
    "controls": [
      "tankSize",
      "gardenUse",
      "roofArea",
      "summerRain",
      "annualRain"
    ],
    "prompt": "Try your own roof, rain, garden and tank size."
  },
  "decide": {
    "compare": [
      {
        "label": "Small 2,000 L tank",
        "set": {
          "tankSize": 2000
        }
      },
      {
        "label": "Middle 5,000 L tank",
        "set": {
          "tankSize": 5000
        }
      },
      {
        "label": "Large 10,000 L tank",
        "set": {
          "tankSize": 10000
        }
      }
    ],
    "tradeoffs": [
      "A bigger tank lasts longer into a dry spell, but costs more and takes up more space.",
      "A small tank fits easily, but fills and overflows in one big storm and empties within days.",
      "Watering less from the tank stretches it further, but the garden may need tap water anyway.",
      "Every tank needs a pump and cleaning, which add cost and effort on top of the tank."
    ],
    "leftOut": [
      "Prices: the article gives no cost for tanks, pumps or tap water, so the model shows water, not money.",
      "Rain is spread evenly across each summer month; real rain comes in bursts, and storms may overflow a small tank.",
      "The dry spell is taken as 60 days and the tank starts it full; both are assumptions.",
      "Garden needs change with plants, soil, shade and heat, not just how you water.",
      "Permits and rules for tanks differ by area; check what applies to you."
    ],
    "questionsToAsk": [
      "Ask your council: do I need a permit for a tank this size?",
      "Ask a tank seller: which pump suits my garden, and what cleaning does it need?",
      "Ask a plumber: how many downpipes can feed the tank, and where can it sit?",
      "Check your weather service: how much rain falls here in a typical summer month?"
    ]
  }
